Z||000004||TRiAD||05-31-2001||12:46 PM||||Jay,<BR>He is using a '98 or '99 Northstar with a '95 (OBD1) computer. They are still looking into ways to modify the ECU to get around some of the "Northstar systems" and such, and hope to have chips and OBD2 ECUs in the future (as well as Turbos), but they're still apparently in somewhat of a development stage. <BR>I believe the company is called "SystemOne" or something. He's in Oklahoma City, and sells complete turn-key packages for around $16K. Only on the Caddy 4 sp auto, no manuals. <BR>It's a nice looking pachage, but even the owner says it's a bit of a pooch off the line. From 50mph on-it rocks. <BR>Hope that helps.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>He's going to be at the El Paso, IL show later this year. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Looking for a white '88 GT 5 sp...<BR>...Could it be...Found?<BR>Stay tuned!</I></B>||||reg||1
